  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vikas Mohan Goel vs State Of Up And Another on 15 March, 2024 High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc:46679 Court No. - 93 Case :- Application U/S 482 No. - 689 of 2024 Applicant :- Vikas Mohan Goel Opposite Party :- State Of Up And Another Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Arun Kumar Singh Deshwal,J. 1.",
    "facts": "2. The present application has been filed for quashing of the entire proceeding of Complaint Case No. 124 of 2022 (State vs. Vikas Mohan Goel), u/s 59(i) of Food Safety Standard Act, 2006, P.S. Dankaur, District Gautam Budh Nagar as well as summoning order dated 17.12.2021, pending before A.C.J.M.-I, Gautam Budh Nagar.",
    "arguments": "3. The contention of learned counsel for the applicant is that the cognizance is barred by Section 200 Cr.P.C. because the cognizance was taken only on the basis of complaint without examining the complainant. 4. Per contra, learned A.G.A. submits that if a complaint is filed by a public servant, then there is no need to examine the complainant."
  },
